+</style>
+<h1>Forklift model review</h1>
+<p>Four findings remain. Production model unchanged. Native Godot 4.7.2 screenshots, captured on desktop in Compatibility and Mobile; these are diagnostic camera views. <a href="../../FORKLIFT_MODEL_REVIEW_2026_10_25.md">Full findings, source locations and limitations</a> · <a href="report.json">Report</a></p>
+<h2>P2 — Reverse fork side-face winding</h2>
+<p>Each fork has 14 side triangles facing opposite their outward normals and 18 inconsistent shared edges. Exterior sides are culled, exposing the opposite inner side. Both detail variants are affected.</p>
+<div class="views">
+<figure><a href="gl_compatibility/fork-side.png"><img src="gl_compatibility/fork-side.png" alt="Fork side profile in Compatibility"></a><figcaption>Compatibility, fork side.</figcaption></figure>
+<figure><a href="gl_compatibility/fork-underside.png"><img src="gl_compatibility/fork-underside.png" alt="Low view beneath the fork blades"></a><figcaption>Compatibility, low underside view.</figcaption></figure>
+<figure><a href="mobile/batched-fork-side.png"><img src="mobile/batched-fork-side.png" alt="Fork side profile after production batching in Mobile"></a><figcaption>Desktop Mobile, production static merger.</figcaption></figure>
+</div>
+<h2>P2 — Flat steering rim disappears from below</h2>
+<p>The hub and spokes remain visible while the single-sided rim vanishes. Replace the flat annulus with a closed round-section rim.</p>
+<div class="views">
+<figure><a href="gl_compatibility/cockpit-top.png"><img src="gl_compatibility/cockpit-top.png" alt="Steering wheel visible from above"></a><figcaption>Compatibility, rim visible from above.</figcaption></figure>
+<figure><a href="gl_compatibility/cockpit-low.png"><img src="gl_compatibility/cockpit-low.png" alt="Steering hub and spokes with the rim missing from below"></a><figcaption>Compatibility, rim missing from below.</figcaption></figure>
+<figure><a href="mobile/batched-cockpit-low.png"><img src="mobile/batched-cockpit-low.png" alt="Missing steering rim in Mobile after production batching"></a><figcaption>Desktop Mobile, same defect after batching.</figcaption></figure>
+</div>
+<h2>P3 — Disconnected chain detail</h2>
+<p>Widely separated blocks do not form a continuous chain, wrap over the pulleys or terminate at the raised carriage.</p>
+<div class="views">
+<figure><a href="gl_compatibility/mast-front.png"><img src="gl_compatibility/mast-front.png" alt="Mast with disconnected chain blocks"></a><figcaption>Compatibility, detailed mast.</figcaption></figure>
+<figure><a href="mobile/batched-mast-front.png"><img src="mobile/batched-mast-front.png" alt="Mast after production batching in Mobile"></a><figcaption>Desktop Mobile, production static merger.</figcaption></figure>
+</div>
+<h2>P3 — Solid exhaust outlet</h2>
+<div class="views">
+<figure><a href="gl_compatibility/exhaust-outlet.png"><img src="gl_compatibility/exhaust-outlet.png" alt="Solid disk at the exhaust tip"></a><figcaption>Compatibility, capped upper stack.</figcaption></figure>
+<figure><a href="mobile/batched-exhaust-outlet.png"><img src="mobile/batched-exhaust-outlet.png" alt="Capped exhaust after production batching in Mobile"></a><figcaption>Desktop Mobile, production static merger.</figcaption></figure>
+</div>
+<h2>Body and rear placement</h2>
+<p>The side skins and arches pass closure, edge orientation and normal checks. The rear crest is clear; the lower fitting is absent.</p>
+<div class="views">
+<figure><a href="gl_compatibility/front-overview.png"><img src="gl_compatibility/front-overview.png" alt="Current Forklift front overview"></a><figcaption>Current model, front.</figcaption></figure>
+<figure><a href="gl_compatibility/rear-overview.png"><img src="gl_compatibility/rear-overview.png" alt="Current Forklift rear with visible crest and no lower fitting"></a><figcaption>Current model, rear.</figcaption></figure>
+<figure><a href="gl_compatibility/rear-full-steering.png"><img src="gl_compatibility/rear-full-steering.png" alt="Forklift rear wheel steering"></a><figcaption>Current model, full rear steering.</figcaption></figure>
+</div>
+<p>No physical-device test or performance certification was performed. Initial diagnostic failure and successful capture logs are retained in <code>logs/</code>.</p>
+</html>
